<title>FRANCE: French GDP rose 0.9 pct in third quarter.</title>
<headline>French GDP rose 0.9 pct in third quarter.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office INSEE gave the following gross domestic product data (base 1980, changes from previous quarters in percent except stocks variation, in billions of 1980 francs.)</p>
<p>					 Q3	 Q2</p>
<p> Total GDP			   0.9     -0.2</p>
<p> Imports			     2.1     -0.5</p>
<p> Exports			     3.1     -1.9</p>
<p> Household consumption	   1.0     -0.9</p>
<p> Investment			  1.0     -0.2</p>
<p> Stocks variation		 -4.3     -1.3</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following more detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>				Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95  Q3 95   1995</p>
<p> Total GDP		   0.9   -0.2     1.1  -0.5    0.2     0.1</p>
<p> Imports		     2.1   -0.5     2.0  -2.0    0.6     0.2</p>
<p> Exports		     3.1   -1.9     4.1  -0.6   -1.6     0.0</p>
<p> Household consumption   1.0   -0.9     2.5  -0.3    0.0     1.6</p>
<p> Public consumption	0.4    0.6     0.4   0.3    0.4     0.2</p>
<p> Investment		  1.0   -0.2    -0.9  -0.3    1.4    -2.0</p>
<p>  - business investment  2.7   -0.9    -0.1  -1.3    1.2    -1.9</p>
<p>  - household investment-2.3    1.8    -1.1   1.0    1.7    -1.9</p>
<p>  - public investment    0.5   -1.5    -4.1   0.4    1.6    -3.0</p>
<p> Stocks variation	 -4.3   -1.3    -8.1  -0.4    6.3     2.1</p>
<p> Internal demand	   0.6    0.3     0.6  -0.9    0.8     0.2</p>
<p>INSEE revised second quarter GDP to a 0.2 percent drop from the 0.4 decline it reported on October 10.</p>
<p>The median forecast of ten economists polled by Reuters last Friday was a rise of 0.9 percent over the second quarter.  </p>
<p>INSEE noted that so-called &quot;acquired growth&quot; for 1994 -- the annual growth that would be recorded if there were no change in the growth rate for the rest of the year -- was 1.2 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
